    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1116">

                <pb facs="0930" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4134.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Nuevo Laredo to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nuevo Laredo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-05T11:00:00-06:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1912—11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Huerta has arrested Villa and sent him to Mexico City for trial. Family of Orozco
                    en route to Europe, he to follow, it is believed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
